Q: Convert a DELETE query with AND and OR logic into CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('who', 5);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('whos', 1);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;or_where('whos', 5);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('who', 1);

$this-&gt;db-&gt;delete('friendconnect');
</code></pre>

<p>This is also an alternative:</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('who', 5)-&gt;where('whos', 1)-&gt;or_where('whos', 5)-&gt;where('who', 1);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;delete('friendconnect');
</code></pre>

<p>This also:</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;where(array('who'=&gt;5, array('whos'=&gt;1)))-&gt;or_where('whos', 5)-&gt;where('who', 1);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;delete('friendconnect');
</code></pre>

<p>More info: <a href="http://www.codeigniter.com/user_guide/database/query_builder.html" rel="noreferrer">here</a></p>

Q: How do I match an element containing two matching child elements with CSS? A: <p>Chaining <code>:has</code> here is the best option to do so:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="false" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>section:has(h2):has(.subtitle) {
  background: red;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;section&gt; &lt;!-- Match --&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;Header text&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;div class="subtitle"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section&gt; &lt;!-- Doesn't match --&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;Header text&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Stream listen() method onDone callback not being called A: <p>Direct use of a stream subscription is the most correct solution.<br />
But sometimes you just want to relax a little and not worry too much about how the subscription works.</p>
<p>This approach allows you not to rely on your knowledge, but allows you to focus more on the result.</p>
<p>Below is one such example.</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>import 'dart:async';

import 'package:multitasking/multitasking.dart';

void main() async {
  for (var i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) {
    final streamController = StreamController&lt;int&gt;();
    final cts = CancellationTokenSource();

    // The same as `stream.listen()`
    // If you need to catch errors, just add a `catch(e) {}`
    unawaited(() async {
      final stream = streamController.stream;
      try {
        await for (final event
            in stream.asCancelable(cts.token, throwIfCanceled: false)) {
          print('Value emitted: $event');
        }
      } finally {
        print('Task done');
      }
    }());

    streamController.add(1);
    await Future&lt;void&gt;.delayed(Duration.zero);
    switch (i) {
      case 0:
        // The same as `subscription.cancel()`
        cts.cancel();
        await streamController.close();
        break;
      case 1:
        await streamController.close();
        // The same as `subscription.cancel()`
        cts.cancel();
        break;
      case 2:
        await streamController.close();
        break;
    }
  }
}

</code></pre>
<p>Results:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>Value emitted: 1
Task done
Value emitted: 1
Task done
Value emitted: 1
Task done
</code></pre>

Q: How to Show and Update hidden div element by hovering on one of three buttons in Javascript? A: <p><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/getElementsByClassName" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>document.getElementsByClassName()</code></a> returns an <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLCollection" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>HTML Collection</code></a>, which is a collection of elements, so saying things like <code>collection.style.display</code> or <code>collection.innerHTML</code> doesn't make a whole lot of sense. I think what you are wanting to do is grab the individual element and update the properties, like so:</p>

<p><code>document.getElementsByClassName("hidden")[0]</code>. </p>

<p>If you need to iterate over the collection, you can access a <code>length</code> property and do a traditional <code>for</code> loop, or you can do an <code>Array.from()</code> using ES6.</p>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function hidepanel() {
  var panel = document.querySelector(".hidden");
  panel.style.display = "none";
}

function updatepanel(x) {
  var desc1 = "Get fully customized workout programs from our dedicated fitness experts.";
  var desc2 = "Nutrional advice and diet plans just for your needs!";
  var desc3 = "Our very own state-of-the-art line of supplementations.Click to Order";
  
  // make variable so we don't have to search the DOM 2 times for every panel
  var hiddenElem = document.querySelector(".hidden"); 
  var panelBody = document.querySelector(".panel-body");
  if (x == 1) {
    hiddenElem.style.display = 'block'; 
    panelBody.innerHTML = 'desc1';
  }
  // don't evaluate unnecessarily
  else if (x == 2) {
    hiddenElem.style.display = 'block'; 
    panelBody.innerHTML = 'desc2';
  }
  // don't evaluate unnecessarily
  else if (x == 3) {
    hiddenElem.style.display = 'block'; 
    panelBody.innerHTML = 'desc3';
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.hidden{
 display: none;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="container"&gt;
  &lt;div class="row anchorbutton"&gt;
    &lt;div class="col-sm-4 col-xs-12 col-md-4 col-lg-4"&gt;
      &lt;a href=#&gt;
        &lt;div class=" mainbuttons b1 text-center" onmouseover="updatepanel(1);" onmouseout="hidepanel()"&gt;Workout Programs
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="col-sm-4 col-md-4 col-lg-4 col-xs-12"&gt;
      &lt;a href=#&gt;
        &lt;div class=" mainbuttons b2 text-center" onmouseover="updatepanel(2);" onmouseout="hidepanel()"&gt; Diet Plans
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="col-sm-4 col-md-4 col-lg-4 col-xs-12 "&gt;
      &lt;a href=#&gt;
        &lt;div class=" mainbuttons  b3 text-center" onmouseover="updatepanel(3);" onmouseout="hidepanel()"&gt; Food Supplements
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="container"&gt;
  &lt;div class="panel panel-default hidden"&gt;
    &lt;div class="hoverable panel-body"&gt; &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

<p>Alternatively, you can use the built in <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/querySelectorAll" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>document.querySelectorAll()</code></a>, which returns a <code>NodeList</code>, which <em>does</em> have a built in iterator function (<code>forEach</code>), which makes iterating over the list cleaner/easier.</p>

<p>That would look like so:</p>

<pre><code>document.querySelectorAll(".hidden").forEach(function (elem) {
  elem.syle.display = "block";
  // etc...
});
</code></pre>

Q: error C2893: Failed to specialize function template &#39;unknown-type std::invoke(_Callable &amp;&amp;,_Types &amp;&amp;...) noexcept(&lt;expr&gt;)&#39; A: <p>You need to provide an object to invoke the non-static method on, like:</p>

<pre><code>auto thread1 = std::thread(&amp;A::solve, b, c);
</code></pre>

<p>But this won't compile either because the method do not match. But you can either cast <code>b</code> to <code>(A*)</code> or change the <code>Boo</code>'s parameter to <code>A* a</code>.</p>

<pre><code>void Boo(A* a, C &amp;c)
{
    auto thread1 = std::thread(&amp;A::solve, a, c);
    thread1.join();
}
</code></pre>

<p>You can look see samples at <a href="http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/invoke" rel="nofollow noreferrer">http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/invoke</a>.</p>

<p>There is similar question <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/44518253/error-c2893failed-to-specialize-function-template-unknown-type-stdinvoke-ca">Error C2893	Failed to specialize function template &#39;unknown-type std::invoke(_Callable &amp;&amp;,_Types &amp;&amp;...)&#39;</a>.</p>
